Laurie Lachlan and Massimo Gianelli have  agreed to plead guilty in the College  Admission scandal the US Attorney's  Office in the District of Massachusetts  announced on Thursday that Laurie will  plead guilty to one count of conspiracy  to commit wire and mail fraud while  Massimo will plead guilty to one count  of conspiracy to commit wire and mail  fraud and honest services wire and mail  fraud if approved by the court Laurie's  plea deal states that she will serve two  months in prison and two years of  supervised release pay a one hundred and  fifty thousand dollar fine and complete  100 hours of community service meanwhile  under Massimo's proposed plea deal he'll  serve five months in prison and two  years of supervised release pay a two  hundred and fifty thousand dollar fine  and complete 250 hours of community  service the date of Laurie and Massimo's  court appearance has not yet been  announced I want to be supportive of  everything they want to do but I do want  them to have somewhat of a normal you  know finish out of high school college  experience maybe because I didn't have  that I really want that for them the  couple was accused of paying five  hundred thousand dollars in bribes to  get their daughters  Olivia Jade and Isabella Rose admitted  to the University of Southern California  as recruits for the crew team even  though neither of them had ever  participated in the sport I want them to  be happy I'm happy to guide them and get  them up and running they initially  pleaded not guilty to all charges  leveled against them claiming their  payments were donations to the school  not bribes overall I am happy and proud  of my girls and I think that they are  nice people and they are kind people and  I think that's the greatest compliment I  can give them the couple's decision to  plead guilty comes nearly two weeks  after a judge rejected the actresses  request to have the charges against her  dropped at the time a source told ET  that Laurie had quote no plans to back  down from her not guilty plea but the  court's decision did make her nervous I  have a lot of mixed emotions  she never in her life thought she would  ever be in this  position and it's almost like a bad  dream she can't wake up from  [Music]
 

